 Sent: Saturday, July 2, 2016 12:14 PM
 Subject: Re: [ballyalley] Re: "New" Blue Ram Unit by Ken

    While the 300 baud interface would be a nice touch, It is NOT necessary to make this unit save and load to either tape or PC.
To use your PC there is some addition software that is available through ballyalley.com.
It has the full 2000 Baud I/O capability that the original Blue RAM had and is compatible with AstroBASIC 2000 Baud. So all of the programs that are saved using 2000 Baud will work including those written with Blue RAM BASIC and ViperSoft BASIC.
It has it's own power supply which also can supply a laptop cooler (advised if you wan t to keep your Arcade from overheating)! Your unit will also have composite video out (NOT COMPONENT video) and pseudo stereo (both sides have the same output) outputs. The original 24 pin ZIF (see ballyalley.com, Blue RAM instructions under Perkins Engineering, extended memory.
All of the latest programs on the UltiMulti Version 2.5 are in this unit as well.
The PCs should be arriving on the 5th of July. They have to be stuffed, labeled, tested packaged and sent out. This will probably take a week to get it ready for shipment. Then 2-3 business days to get to you. I an going to be at the Cleveland Computer, Arcade and Gaming (CCAG) show along with Mike White on July
23, 2016. If you have the means to get there we would love to meet you in person. If I know you're coming, I will bring your unit there to show it off and give it to you!

Ken Lill

