I have 2 that work well. The one I like most is the Targus "Chill Pad" model PA248 U. It draws 28mA, is exceptionally quiet and can lie on any flat surface because it draws its air from a slot on the back side. The second I got off of the internet. It in made by Sakar. It is called simply "USB Cooler" and draws a whopping 300mA. Although it is slightly noisier, it does have a substantially greater air flow. However, It is at the TOP of the current flow I would recommend for use of the RWB because the INS8154 uses quite a lot of current when operating. There are many out there and they range from about $15.00 to about $45.00. Please mind the current flow. anything above 200mA is going to be pushing the power supply if you have the I/O option.
Ken



